      "rationale": "The art and science of designing buildings. This answer is supported by the checked Batch 056 local raw PDF source families for The Triple Nature of Architecture.",
      "explanation": "This suggests an impossible choice. Responsible architecture must integrate all three dimensions; neither should be sacrificed. Beauty does not compensate for structural inadequacy or functional failure; the design has failed fundamentally. This contradicts the fundamental principle that architecture requires simultaneous excellence in all dimensions. A design that is beautiful but unable to function safely or serve its purpose has failed in its essential task. All three dimensions—firmitas (structural safety), utilitas (fitness for flood conditions), and venustas (beauty)—must be present and integrated.",
